    {
      "filename": "Plan of the Gobindgarh Fort near the formidable wall (38939184591).jpg",
      "title": "File:Plan of the Gobindgarh Fort near the formidable wall (38939184591).jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c8/Plan_of_the_Gobindgarh_Fort_near_the_formidable_wall_%2838939184591%29.jpg",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Plan_of_the_Gobindgarh_Fort_near_the_formidable_wall_(38939184591).jpg",
      "width": 4032,
      "height": 3024,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0",
      "artist": "shankar s. from Dubai, united arab emirates",
      "description": "As we pass the formidable walls of the Gobindgarh Fort and the nearly vertical steps leading onto it, we also notice a large billboard showing the plan/ map of the fort. After being closed to the public for several years, as it had been under the control of the Indian army until very recently (see notes earlier in this album), a bit of restoration and tourist oriented features have been added. So apart from being a plan of the fort premises, this signboard also points out the location of various facilities like the toilet, food court etc. (Amritsar, Punjab, northern India, Nov. 2017)",
      "dateCreated": "2017-12-01 00:00",
      "categories": [
        "CC-BY-2.0",
        "Flickr images reviewed by FlickreviewR 2",
        "Gobindgarh Fort",
        "Photographs by shankar s."
      ],
      "sourceType": "commons-category",
      "sourceArticleId": "gobindgarh-fort-wp",
      "sourceGeohash4": "ttt5",
